          "statement_id": "SYS-PORTFOLIO-001-FIL-0046-STMT-000027",
          "line": 180
        },
        "claim": "On an 'INIT' request the system opens the process-sequence and batch-control files for update, clears the in-memory sequence table and process count, and positions the process-sequence file at the first key greater than or equal to the requested process date ('No sequence found for date' is reported if none). It then reads every following process definition; when a definition's type (PSR-TYPE) equals the sequence type requested by the caller (LS-SEQUENCE-TYPE), it adds 1 to the process count and appends the process ID with sequence number equal to that count and status READY ('R'); otherwise the definition is skipped. No check is made against the 100-entry table limit. For each table entry it then writes one batch-control record with the process ID as job name, the requested process date, the sequence number and status READY ('Error creating control record' is reported on a write failure)."
      },
